{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many","id":1097697,"title":"How Many?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-27T23:27:20-07:00","id":1097697,"title":"How Many?","content":"This question has probably been asked many times .. and its likely in the book somewhere .. so how many Scions of each god are there? one or many? I there only one Scion of Thor at a time? The reason I ask is that in the legends and myths some of them gods were rather promiscuous in there dealings with mortals and sired quite a few children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T23:43:10-07:00","id":1097700,"title":"","content":"Depends on the god, to be honest. Some might not have any at a given point in time, some might only have one, and some might have quite a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T05:11:01-07:00","id":1097751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many#post1097697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question has probably been asked many times .. and its likely in the book somewhere .. so how many Scions of each god are there? one or many? I there only one Scion of Thor at a time? The reason I ask is that in the legends and myths some of them gods were rather promiscuous in there dealings with mortals and sired quite a few children.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's somewhat ambiguous. In first edition, one of the antagonist Scions is surprised and curious to find out they have a long lost half sibling who's also a Scion. Which could suggest that multiple (active) Scions under the same deity is either an uncommon occurrence, or that the Scions are intentionally left in the dark as to their extended relatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T07:43:39-07:00","id":1097772,"title":"","content":"Hmm ok ... was curious. Thanks for answers<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T00:40:19-07:00","id":1098368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many?p=1097751#post1097751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's somewhat ambiguous. In first edition, one of the antagonist Scions is surprised and curious to find out they have a long lost half sibling who's also a Scion. Which could suggest that multiple (active) Scions under the same deity is either an uncommon occurrence, or that the Scions are intentionally left in the dark as to their extended relatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIf it is the Scion I think you are talking about... it was actually a twin sister/brother she had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T00:44:05-07:00","id":1098370,"title":"","content":"I believe the canon answer is something like &quot;more than you think, but many of them never see a Visitation, and many of those that do die well before reaching Demigod.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"use