class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIf it is the Scion I think you are talking about... it was actually a twin sister/brother she had.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one with the magical sex changing skin suit, and the one who regularly mutilates herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T16:17:00-07:00","id":1099320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many?p=1098391#post1098391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> According to the Companion book, Sun Wukong doesn't even keep tabs on the women he sleeps with until somebody informs him he has a kid he didn't know about. Then he goes to pay them a visit. Then there's Zeus, who the majority of Greek Heroes that I'm familiar with claim him as their father.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The one with the magical sex changing skin suit, and the one who regularly mutilates herself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that whole mess was partially brought about by the parent in question keeping them both in the dark. Demigod also mentions that if the group isn't using the premade PCs and one of the hero level NPCs has the same parent to let that play out in whatever kind of sibling dynamic is the most interesting. And Ragnorok has an adventure that assumes there are tow different scions of Odin in the party.<br /> <br /> So ultimatly it seems to come down to the god in question, how long a given scion survives, who the gods bother visiting, and I assum at least some low level scions might get a visitation but no birthrights to speak of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:10:36-07:00","id":1099476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many?p=1099320#post1099320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But that whole mess was partially brought about by the parent in question keeping them both in the dark. Demigod also mentions that if the group isn't using the premade PCs and one of the hero level NPCs has the same parent to let that play out in whatever kind of sibling dynamic is the most interesting. And Ragnorok has an adventure that assumes there are tow different scions of Odin in the party.<br /> <br /> So ultimatly it seems to come down to the god in question, how long a given scion survives, who the gods bother visiting, and I assum at least some low level scions might get a visitation but no birthrights to speak of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which is why I said multiple Scions are either rare, or the children typically don't know about them. Which would actually make sense. I mean, wouldn't it be very awkward to receive your visitation, be told you have a great and promising destiny, and then for them to just start rambling off your extended family members? That's not something that just comes up in casual conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T06:16:30-07:00","id":1099479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many?p=1099476#post1099476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why I said multiple Scions are either rare, or the children typically don't know about them. Which would actually make sense. I mean, wouldn't it be very awkward to receive your visitation, be told you have a great and promising destiny, and then for them to just start rambling off your extended family members? That's not something that just comes up in casual conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I consider &quot;Older half sibling&quot; to be one of the easiest guides to work into a backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T09:03:14-07:00","id":1099538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1097697-how-many?p=1099479#post1099479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I consider &quot;Older half sibling&quot; to be one of the easiest guides to work into a backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, sure, that could definitely work. But that doesn't mean you'd be aware of <i>every half sibling</i> unless you specifically asked for them; or your divine parent just felt like bragging about every Scion they're currently sponsoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T15:05:49-07:00","id":1099657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <s